{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966808,"nonce":"xzOOZi/6+nbxoRW3jAIiEgAi7CI=","title":"Web runner swallowed right-clicks unless a text input owned focus. mousedown listener","message":"On web (wasm), right-clicking anywhere on a Blinc canvas page that didn't have a focused text input did nothing. Hosts that wired `Div::on_right_click(|evt| ...)` — node-editor's `cn::context_menu()` opener, canvas-kit demos that paint their own surface — got no callback. Desktop was unaffected; the same code worked there.\n\n\nTwo listeners in `crates/blinc_app/src/web.rs` together swallowed the gesture:\n\n1. **mousedown filter** (~line 1187): `if evt.button() != 0 { return; }` — drops right-click + middle-click before they reach `dispatch_mouse_down`. The comment justifies it as \"right-click is owned by the contextmenu listener below.\"\n\n2. **contextmenu listener** (~line 1648–1668) → `handle_context_menu`. The handler early-returned when `focused_editable_node_id()` was `None`. The early-return comment claimed \"let the click pass through to normal mouse_down handling\" — but step 1 had already dropped that.\n\nSo the only path the gesture could reach the layout / event router was through a focused editable widget. Hosts without one were silently inert.\n\n\nInside `handle_context_menu`, when no editable is focused, synthesize a right-button POINTER_DOWN + POINTER_UP through `dispatch_mouse_down` / `dispatch_mouse_up`. The Div filter in `blinc_layout` keys `on_right_click` off `mouse_button == 2`, so this fires the host's handler immediately. Pairing the DOWN with an UP keeps the event router's pressed-target tracking from stranding the canvas in a half-pressed state.\n\nWhen a focused editable IS present, keep the historical edit-menu (Cut / Copy / Paste) path.\n\n\nThe winit / windowed runner doesn't have an intercept analogous to the browser's `contextmenu` listener. Right-button POINTER_DOWN flows straight into the event router → Div::on_right_click handlers fire. The intercept was specific to the browser needing `preventDefault()` to suppress its own menu, and the early-return was a bad assumption about who owns the gesture.\n\n\nCompanion to [[gotcha-path-overlay-msaa-only-dispatch]] — same session symptom report (web node_editor demo broken in several ways) but distinct root cause. That one was missing PATH content; this one was the missing RIGHT-CLICK gesture.","files":null}]}